{"id": "Q-066", "kind": "q_deep_read", "ok": true, "chars": 3824, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 2200, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1172}, "prompt_tokens": 2095, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "total_tokens": 4295}, "secs": 66.6, "text": "# Chunk 67 Analysis — Posts 4246–4298 (March 28, 2019)\n\n## Context: Post-Mueller Report Window\n\nThis chunk lands on the day after the Barr letter summarizing the Mueller Report was released (March 24, 2019) and amid the aftermath. Q is repositioning from \"Mueller is actually working for Trump\" anticipation to pivoting toward FISA declassification, Smollett prosecution, and anti-Schiff narratives.\n\n---\n\n## (1) SPECIFIC DATED OR CHECKABLE CLAIMS\n\n### News Media / Event Links\n\n| Post | Claim/Reference | Checkable Element |\n|------|----------------|-------------------|\n| **4254** | Fox News: Trump vows to release FISA docs post-Mueller; slams \"treasonous FBI\" | URL verifiable; FISA declassification did not fully materialize in this form |\n| **4255** | Fox News: Internal emails from Foxx's office show push to defend dropping Smollett charges | URL verifiable; foreshadows federal prosecution which occurred (16-count indictment dropped, federal probe followed) |\n| **4261** | Trump tweet #1111217169730338816 calling for Schiff's resignation | Tweet verifiable; Schiff did not resign |\n| **4262** | Doug Collins tweet #1111256323008708608; directs to \"[Page 17]\" | Likely refers to Page 17 of the Nunes memo or Collins's declassified transcript release |\n| **4263** | Fox News piece re: Eric Holder \"when did you think America was great\" | URL verifiable |\n| **4266** | Fox News: Twitter may annotate tweets from elected officials violating rules | URL verifiable; Twitter label policy for politicians was publicly discussed at this time |\n| **4267** | Paul Sperry tweet #1111307392438943744 | Journalist tweet; likely about FISA/DOJ corruption |\n| **4279** | Trump tweet #1111214993293357056: \"FBI & DOJ to review the outrageous Jussie Smollett case\" | Tweet verifiable; DOJ did open review |\n| **4280** | Ben Carson tweet #1111218929337290753 | Linked as an apparent \"confirmation\" signal |\n| **4284** | John Solomon tweet/report #1111310208486252545 | Solomon was actively publishing FISA-related stories in this window |\n\n### Legal/Statutory References\n\n| Post | Reference | Content |\n|------|-----------|---------|\n| **4272** | 18 U.S.C. Chapter 115 | **Treason, Sedition, and Subversive Activities** — provided without commentary as implied legal framework for targets |\n| **4261** | \"[Knowingly] disseminating FALSE information is illegal\" | Implies 18 U.S.C. §§ 1001 (false statements) or related statutes |\n\n### Predictions / Forward-Looking Claims\n\n| Post | Claim | Outcome |\n|------|-------|---------|\n| **4255** | \"FEDS (DOJ) will prosecute? >It shall be done\" | DOJ review occurred; no federal charges ultimately filed against Smollett |\n| **4279** | \">It shall be done\" (echoing 4255) | Self-reinforcing loop |\n| **4261** | \"Leaking investigations can lead to [forced] resignations\" | No forced resignations from this specific chain materialized |\n| **4280** | \"1st of many?\" (re: Ben Carson tweet framed as USA v. LifeLog) | No \"LifeLog\" prosecution occurred; LifeLog was a DARPA program cancelled in 2004; cryptic comparison to Facebook/data harvesting |\n\n### Diagrammed Claim (4270)\n\n```\n[NO NAME][MEDIA - [JB][JC] LEAKS —→ POTUS Daily Brief/FBI]\n```\n\n- **[NO NAME]** = John McCain (established Q convention)\n- **[JB]** = John Brennan (implied)\n- **[JC]** = James Comey (implied)\n- **Claim:** Leaks from Brennan/Comey, routed through media, connected to POTUS's Daily Brief and FBI. Asks \"Match?\" inviting anons to confirm pattern.\n- This is a checkable claim only in the sense that leak-pattern reporting (Solomon, Sperry) could be cross-referenced, but the diagram itself asserts an undisclosed operational chain.\n\n---\n\n## (2) RECURRING SYMBOLS AND PHRASES\n\n### Bracket Designator System\n\n| Designator | Posts | Meaning (inferred) |\n|-----------|-------|-------------------|\n| **[Knowingly]** | 426"}
